WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:16.091
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June twenty-first. For high-school students looking for work, this is the best job market on record — there are more openings than ever. Let's listen.

00:00:16.692 --> 00:00:19.452
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:27.832
<v News>来年の春に高校を卒業する人の就職が、とても良い状況です。

00:00:28.532 --> 00:00:36.787
<v News>会社が「働いてほしい」と言う数が、高校生一人に対してたくさんあります。

00:00:37.487 --> 00:00:44.496
<v News>一人の高校生に、平均で4つ以上の仕事があるそうです。

00:00:45.195 --> 00:00:53.619
<v News>これは、調査を始めた1988年から、一番多い数です。

00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:00.344
<v News>理由は、多くの会社で、人手が足りないからです。

00:01:01.043 --> 00:01:07.115
<v News>日本では、若い人の数が少しずつ減っています。

00:01:07.816 --> 00:01:14.512
<v News>だから、会社は高校生にも、来てほしいと思っています。

00:01:15.212 --> 00:01:22.436
<v News>給料を、大学を出た人と同じくらいに上げる会社も出てきました。

00:01:23.135 --> 00:01:30.096
<v News>高校生にとっては、仕事を選びやすい、うれしいニュースです。

00:01:30.796 --> 00:01:32.427
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:33.028 --> 00:01:41.811
<v Slow>来年の春に高校を卒業する人の就職が、とても良い状況です。

00:01:42.611 --> 00:01:47.243
<v Host>Job-hunting looks very good for people graduating high school next spring.

00:01:47.843 --> 00:01:50.316
<v Vocab>就職

00:01:50.715 --> 00:01:56.355
<v Host>It means finding a job, or employment — landing your first position after finishing school.

00:01:56.956 --> 00:02:06.388
<v Slow>会社が「働いてほしい」と言う数が、高校生一人に対してたくさんあります。

00:02:07.188 --> 00:02:12.756
<v Host>There are many companies saying 'we want you to work for us' for each single high-school student.

00:02:13.355 --> 00:02:15.804
<v Vocab>働く

00:02:16.204 --> 00:02:21.580
<v Host>It means to work. A related noun means labor — the work itself.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:30.171
<v Slow>一人の高校生に、平均で4つ以上の仕事があるそうです。

00:02:30.972 --> 00:02:36.372
<v Host>I hear there are, on average, more than four jobs for each high-school student.

00:02:36.972 --> 00:02:39.276
<v Vocab>仕事

00:02:39.675 --> 00:02:45.123
<v Host>It means a job, or work — what you do all day, and what you look for when job-hunting.

00:02:45.723 --> 00:02:55.348
<v Slow>これは、調査を始めた1988年から、一番多い数です。

00:02:56.147 --> 00:03:00.563
<v Host>This is the highest number since the survey began in nineteen eighty-eight.

00:03:01.163 --> 00:03:03.204
<v Vocab>数

00:03:03.604 --> 00:03:09.027
<v Host>It means number or count — here, the number of jobs available for each student.

00:03:09.627 --> 00:03:16.491
<v Slow>理由は、多くの会社で、人手が足りないからです。

00:03:17.292 --> 00:03:21.036
<v Host>The reason is that many companies don't have enough workers.

00:03:21.635 --> 00:03:23.795
<v Vocab>人手

00:03:24.195 --> 00:03:31.443
<v Host>It means manpower, or helping hands. Being short of hands is a phrase you'll hear all over Japan now.

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:38.979
<v Slow>日本では、若い人の数が少しずつ減っています。

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:44.436
<v Host>In Japan, the number of young people is gradually decreasing.

00:03:45.036 --> 00:03:47.003
<v Vocab>減る

00:03:47.403 --> 00:03:53.211
<v Host>It means to decrease, to go down in number. It's the opposite of the verb meaning to increase.

00:03:53.812 --> 00:04:01.467
<v Slow>だから、会社は高校生にも、来てほしいと思っています。

00:04:02.268 --> 00:04:07.259
<v Host>So companies want high-school students, too, to come and join them.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.996
<v Vocab>思う

00:04:10.395 --> 00:04:16.684
<v Host>It means to think, or to feel — the verb you reach for to give an opinion, as in 'I think that ....'

00:04:17.283 --> 00:04:25.540
<v Slow>給料を、大学を出た人と同じくらいに上げる会社も出てきました。

00:04:26.339 --> 00:04:32.339
<v Host>Some companies have even started raising pay to about the same as university graduates get.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.244
<v Vocab>給料

00:04:35.644 --> 00:04:42.220
<v Host>It means salary, or pay. The day it lands is payday, and when it climbs, you've gotten a raise.

00:04:42.819 --> 00:04:45.819
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:49.180
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:04:49.879 --> 00:04:57.560
<v News>来年の春に高校を卒業する人の就職が、とても良い状況です。

00:04:58.259 --> 00:05:06.516
<v News>会社が「働いてほしい」と言う数が、高校生一人に対してたくさんあります。

00:05:07.216 --> 00:05:14.223
<v News>一人の高校生に、平均で4つ以上の仕事があるそうです。

00:05:14.923 --> 00:05:23.348
<v News>これは、調査を始めた1988年から、一番多い数です。

00:05:24.048 --> 00:05:30.072
<v News>理由は、多くの会社で、人手が足りないからです。

00:05:30.771 --> 00:05:36.843
<v News>日本では、若い人の数が少しずつ減っています。

00:05:37.543 --> 00:05:44.240
<v News>だから、会社は高校生にも、来てほしいと思っています。

00:05:44.939 --> 00:05:52.163
<v News>給料を、大学を出た人と同じくらいに上げる会社も出てきました。

00:05:52.863 --> 00:05:59.824
<v News>高校生にとっては、仕事を選びやすい、うれしいニュースです。

00:06:00.524 --> 00:06:03.259
<v Host>Quiz time. Three questions.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:12.403
<v Slow>来年の春に高校を卒業する人の就職は、どんな状況ですか。

00:06:13.204 --> 00:06:20.668
<v Host>What's the job situation for people graduating high school next spring? Very good — lots of openings for each student.

00:06:21.267 --> 00:06:28.228
<v Slow>高校生一人に、平均でいくつの仕事がありますか。

00:06:29.028 --> 00:06:34.500
<v Host>On average, how many jobs are there per high-school student? More than four.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:40.596
<v Slow>仕事がたくさんある理由は、何ですか。

00:06:41.396 --> 00:06:47.923
<v Host>Why are there so many jobs? Because companies are short of workers, and young people are decreasing.

00:06:48.524 --> 00:07:00.908
<v Host>That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

00:07:01.507 --> 00:07:03.764
<v News>また明日。
